.TH OPEN-RAILS 6 "2026" "open-rails-linux" "Games"
.SH NAME
open\-rails \- native Linux train simulator for Microsoft Train Simulator content
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B open\-rails
.RI [ arguments ]
.br
.B fts
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A train simulator that reads Microsoft Train Simulator routes, activities, rolling stock and
sounds, built as a native Linux program rather than run under Wine.
.PP
.B open\-rails
starts the simulator itself. With no arguments it continues with the selections from the last
session; it is what the desktop entry runs.
.PP
.B fts
is the launcher: it manages content folders, lists what they contain, and starts a run. It is
the usual way in.
.SH LAUNCHER COMMANDS
.TP
.B fts content
List the configured content folders.
.TP
.BI "fts content add " "name path"
Add a folder holding Microsoft Train Simulator content and scan it.
.TP
.BI "fts content remove " name
Remove a folder.
.TP
.B fts content refresh
Rescan every folder. Do this after adding or changing routes on disk.
.TP
.BI "fts routes [" folder ]
List routes.
.TP
.BI "fts activities " route
List a route's activities.
.TP
.BI "fts paths " route
List a route's player paths.
.TP
.BI "fts consists [" folder ]
List consists.
.TP
.BI "fts play " "route activity"
Start an activity.
.TP
.BI "fts explore " "route path consist"
Start an explore session. Accepts
.BI \-\-time " HH:MM" \fR,
.BI \-\-season " summer"
and
.BI \-\-weather " clear" \fR.
.TP
.B fts resume
Continue the last save.
.TP
.B fts doctor
Check that this machine can run the simulator and report what is missing.
.PP
Routes, activities, paths and consists are matched on their name, case insensitively; a unique
prefix is enough.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FTS_MSTS_PATH
Where Microsoft Train Simulator is installed. Set this when the content is somewhere the
automatic search would not look; it checks the XDG data directory, the home directory and the
Program Files folder of any Wine or Proton prefix.
.TP
.B OPEN_RAILS_VULKAN
Set to 1 to run the OpenGL renderer on Vulkan through Mesa's zink driver.
.TP
.B FTS_ACTIVITYRUNNER
Path to the simulator binary, for running the launcher against a build directory.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/open\-rails\-linux
Settings and profiles.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/open\-rails\-linux
Saves.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/open\-rails\-linux/Logs
Logs. Attach these to a bug report.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/open\-rails\-linux
Scanned content indexes. Safe to delete; they are rebuilt on the next scan.
.PP
These follow the XDG base directory specification and move with the corresponding
.BR XDG_ *_HOME
variables.
.SH NOTES
Microsoft Train Simulator content refers to its own files with inconsistent capitalisation,
which NTFS forgives and Linux file systems do not. The simulator resolves those references case
insensitively, so a route copied from a Windows machine loads unchanged.
.PP
A RailDriver desk needs read access to its hidraw device. The package installs a udev rule
granting it to the
.B input
group; add yourself to that group and log back in.
.SH SEE ALSO
The documentation installed under
.IR /usr/share/doc/open\-rails\-linux .
.SH BUGS
Report at
.UR https://github.com/agustinluzardo/Open-Rails-Linux-Fork/issues
.UE .
